 "title": "What not-all-equal forces",
 "status": "Partial",
 "claim": "L1: under NAE nothing is frozen, every tie is an equality or an inequality, every emergent knot forbids one complementary pair (a plain or signed NAE). L2: a Pasch forces NAE on its four complementary triples. L3: a book of any number of pages is read faithfully. L4: the weighted cut (weights = knots per pair) is at most twice the number of knots, with equality exactly at states; hence lambda-fold weaves' states cut two thirds of co-knotted pairs and 2-(v,3,lambda) designs have no state for v > 4.",
 "dependencies": [
  "KNOTS-ALONE-20261111-001A"
 ],
